# Task 4.3: Multi-Channel Notification Engine

**Owner:** Backend Engineer | **Risk:** MEDIUM | **Sprint:** 4

---

## Sub-Tasks

### A. Deno Edge Functions
- [ ] Author `supabase/functions/on-complaint-created/index.ts`
  - Triggered by `complaints` INSERT webhook
  - Identifies shift-active manager via `on_call_schedules` query
  - Dispatches in-app notification with `secure_link_id` (ZERO PHI)
- [ ] Author `supabase/functions/on-sla-breach/index.ts`
  - Triggered by `sla_breach_log` INSERT webhook
  - Dispatches SMS + email escalation to on-call manager
  - Embeds TRAI/DLT Template ID in every SMS payload
- [ ] Author `supabase/functions/nightly-compliance-audit/index.ts`
  - Scheduled via `pg_cron` at 02:30 IST nightly
  - Checks: 24h acknowledgment breaches, NULL escalations, stuck `investigating` tickets, CAPA gaps

### B. Zero-PHI Enforcement
- [ ] ALL notification channels (email, SMS, in-app) transmit ZERO patient data
- [ ] Only `secure_link_id` transmitted — requires authenticated session to resolve details
- [ ] Validate: inspect raw SMS/email payload — no description, name, or contact fields

### C. 1-Click Deep-Link Acknowledgment
- [ ] Build `src/app/api/acknowledge/route.ts` POST handler
- [ ] Generate JWT-signed deep-link token: single-use UUID, 15-min TTL
- [ ] On valid click: `UPDATE complaints SET status = 'acknowledged'`
- [ ] Cancel Inngest SLA timer: `inngest.send("complaint/resolved")`
- [ ] Set `notifications.status = 'Read'`
- [ ] Rate limit: 5 req/min on `/api/acknowledge` via Redis Token Bucket
- [ ] Replay protection: consumed tokens return `403 — token already consumed`

### D. TRAI/DLT SMS Compliance
- [ ] MSG91 as primary SMS gateway — configure via [.env](file:///c:/Application%20V4.0/.env) (`MSG91_API_KEY`, `MSG91_SENDER_ID`)
- [ ] Twilio as fallback — configure via [.env](file:///c:/Application%20V4.0/.env) (`TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID`, `TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN`)
- [ ] Pre-approved DLT Template IDs embedded in every SMS payload
- [ ] Fallback logic: if MSG91 returns error, retry once via Twilio

### E. Shift-Aware Routing & Idempotency
- [ ] Query `on_call_schedules` before dispatching any notification
- [ ] If no active shift found → default to Quality Coordinator
- [ ] Check `processed_events` BEFORE dispatching — prevent duplicates on Edge Function retry
- [ ] INSERT `processed_events` entry AFTER successful dispatch

---

**Deliverable:** E2E demo — breach → shift-aware SMS → 1-click acknowledge → SLA timer stops
